From eae8c79c09ad68aa3e27ab6ce0d8124ac1dc0aef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stew Forster <ci@rdna-boosts.invalid>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 17:07:27 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] crash #373 fix (candidate), part 3: A -- the VMM pool's
 peer grant is BEST EFFORT, exactly as the slab's already is

cuMemSetAccess over all peer descriptors in ONE call meant a single refused descriptor (the driver cannot build a
peer mapping once the MoE arena has taken the VRAM) poisoned the grant and aborted the process; it was invisible
while one context existed because its pools are grown during load, and the pair adds a SECOND context whose pools
grow at request time -- measured 'HipVMM Failure: invalid argument' in ggml_cuda_pool_vmm::alloc from mul_mat_q,
~2 s in, only with the arena on and only with the pair.  Now: grant the OWNER's descriptor alone (located
explicitly -- the list is in device order, so the owner is not always first), then each peer alone, keep the mask of
what was granted and the ranges in a registry, and let the copy predicate answer for pool destinations too
(ggml_cuda_slab_peer_copy_ok -> ggml_cuda_peer_copy_ok, slab AND pool).  A refused peer stages through host memory.

Also: the async-input origin uploads on a private non-blocking stream instead of the cudaStreamPerThread sentinel
(HIP couples that to the legacy default stream, so a peer arm's capture refuses it: measured as a failed set_input in
llm_graph_input_ple on the host tier).  Ordering was already carried by events, never by the handle.

Host tier now clean end to end (2 rounds of 71k + 23k + 800-token generation, -ncmoe 48) with the decode context's
declared reserve raised (MOE_EXPERT_CACHE_AUX_RESERVE_MIB=6144; the flat 3584 MiB is not enough there -- TODO #366
is a hard blocker for the host tier, not a cost item).  Resident config unchanged: 2 rounds clean, soak gate 11/11.
